# 2026-09-01: twins created or grown by the prevention-gate work. Reasons are
# specific; the two worth merging are recorded in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F3.
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-torch-venv.sh | linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-torch-venv.sh | 65 | assert_pinned_versions / assert_app_venv_parity: each gate must read standalone in its own failure output
linux/scripts/01-core/chain-lifecycle.sh | linux/scripts/01-core/chain-lifecycle.sh | 25 | chain_status_kv_json / _list_json walk the same CSV; worth ONE walker -- see refactoring-backlog F3
linux/scripts/tests/test-disk-guard.sh | linux/scripts/tests/test-disk-guard.sh | 30 | two fixture builders; explicit beats shared in a test that must not hide its own setup
linux/scripts/01-core/disk-guard.sh | linux/scripts/01-core/disk-guard.sh | 26 | keep_n arg validation in the trim and the watch entry points; both are public and validate independently
linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | 24 | numeric-knob guards in the lane gate and the disk watcher; same idiom, different knobs
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-stage-build.sh | linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | 27 | the free-space-vs-threshold guard; same idiom, different knob and failure text
linux/scripts/01-core/disk-guard.sh | linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | 24 | as above: the caller re-validates the knob it passes in
linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | 24 | the test EVALs the shipped function; overlap with the implementation is the point
linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | linux/scripts/tests/test-parallel-loop.sh | 20 | is_truthy stub: a test that sources platform.sh could no longer prove the shipped copy
linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | linux/scripts/tests/test-ffmpeg-dnn-contract.sh | 20 | is_truthy stub, as above
linux/scripts/01-core/platform.sh | linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | 20 | is_truthy: the test stub deliberately mirrors the canonical definition
linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | linux/scripts/verify-shipped-wrapper.sh | 20 | _is_truthy: verify-shipped-wrapper runs standalone; sourcing platform.sh is the fix -- backlog F3
linux/scripts/01-core/runtime-build-fns.sh | linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | 14 | reviewed 2026-09-02: `usage() { cat <<'EOF'` plus two option lines the chain orchestrator documents identically. NOT deliberate so much as unfinished — build-cross-chain.sh could call runtime_shared_usage_options too; it was left out because it is a different flow (stage chain, not runtime) and merging its help needs its own review. Budget pinned so the overlap cannot grow
docs/upstream/windows-containers-lsm-session-event-hang.md | docs/upstream/windows-containers-lsm-session-event-hang.md | 16 | reviewed 2026-09-02: the file repeats ITSELF -- the same Windows-Containers issue reference appears in the summary at the top and again in the reference list at the bottom, which is how an upstream write-up is supposed to read. It is a WINDOWS-lane document and the standing rule here is to note, not edit, Windows content from the Linux lane, so the budget is pinned rather than the prose reflowed
linux/scripts/01-core/compiler-resolution.sh | linux/scripts/03-media/android-build-preamble.sh | 64 | reviewed 2026-09-02: the BOOTSTRAP PARADOX. android-build-preamble.sh sources the canonical 01-core/compiler-resolution.sh when present and falls back to an inline copy when it is not — a fallback that must duplicate the thing it stands in for, or it is not a fallback. Consolidating the iree+litert copies into the preamble did not create this overlap, it made a pre-existing one visible in ONE place instead of two
linux/scripts/03-media/android-build-preamble.sh | linux/scripts/03-media/build/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-probe-framework.sh | 30 | reviewed 2026-09-02: same host-compiler-preference logic, fourth site. See the compiler-resolution entry above — this is a FAMILY (canonical + preamble fallback + ffmpeg probe + iree native), not a pair, and wants one owner
